{"input_domain":["Generation8 ordinary double battle; all four seats alive and near. User at seat0 starts with current WATER type, active PROTEAN, valid ordinary CURSE slot, HP101/101 and positive PP. A CURSE-capable GENGAR can have this current type via SOAK and PROTEAN via allowed Skill Swap; this review assumes the already-established legal state and does not claim execution of that acquisition chain.","User Attack/Defense/Speed stages are zero and their changes permitted, so the initial non-Ghost Curse whole-use gate passes. User and targets retain their types/state during this use except the intended Protean change.","Foes at seats1 and3 are uncursed, with seat1 Follow Me marker1 established by a valid earlier action and seat3 unmarked. Fixed random foe selection chooses seat3. No Spotlight/other redirection, Stalwart/Propeller Tail, semi-invulnerability, Magic Coat/Bounce, move blocking, Substitute/protection, type-data gaps, healing item, ability suppression or other callback state changes. Normal feedback/animation return."],"ordinary_control":["Change only the starting user current type to GHOST: initial target construction already uses RandomNearFoe, fixed choice seat3 is redirected by Follow Me to seat1, Protean does not alter the type, seat1 is cursed and user HP becomes51.","Remove only active Protean from the WATER-start fixture: initial target remains User/empty and the non-Ghost general effect requests Speed−1 then Attack+1 then Defense+1; no Curse HP cost and neither foe is cursed."],"minimal_counterexample":{"EXACT_VALUE_ALREADY_DISPLAYED_AT":"/normative_records/15/bidirectional_evidence/fact_consumer_chain/state_observation_and_later_result"},"failure_cancel_partial_commit":{"partial_commits_under_cancellation":["At initial whole-use failure because all three non-Ghost stage requests are unavailable, ordinary PP/history are already committed, while the later Protean change/reconstruction/Curse/HP cost have not occurred.","Once the late Protean change has happened, it is not locally rolled back if the rebuilt target is already cursed or if an unrelated later callback fails; ordinary PP/history and any reached type write remain.","For a successful Curse target main effect, the target mark precedes user HP expenditure and HP-item check. An exception/cancellation after a reached write does not justify undoing that prefix. This proposal does not specify host recovery, continued process execution or diagnostic retries."]},"impact":{"EXACT_VALUE_ALREADY_DISPLAYED_AT":"/normative_records/15/identity_and_verdict/severity_reason"},"evidence_levels_and_execution":{"evidence_level":"STATIC_SOURCE_READ + STATIC_CONTROL_FLOW_DERIVATION; not isolated-reference, independent-model or full-host/Demo execution"}}
